A||||7||ponya||Rear deck lid bowing?||||5||
Z||000000||ponya||09-04-2000||05:21 PM||||Trying to adjust my rear deck lid today. Left side by the vent is up, but can be pushed down. Not being held up by anything underneath. Do the deck lids have a history of bowing from the heat? If so, I'll leave it alone. Any info appreciated.     Bob||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||09-04-2000||09:53 PM||||The deck vent panels have screws that hold them down in place.  The passenger side (above the battery) has a screw with a tab on it so you can turn it by hand.  The other side has a regular screw the is removed with a flat bladed screwdriver.  The screws fit into a clip that is around the bracket they mount into.  You have either lost the screw or the clip they mount into. <P>It would take an awful lot of heat to warp the vent panels.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||09-04-2000||10:22 PM||||Sounds like he's talking about the deck lid, not the vent.<P>Ponya--I seem to have the same problem.  Either mine has gotten out of adjustment (in the exact same place) or it's warped/bowed.  I'll try to adjust it in the spring.  If I can't, I'll have to break down and buy another decklid.  The good news is that I have a notchback and the decklids seem to be more plentiful (and cheaper) than the fastback lids.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||09-04-2000||10:52 PM||||Yeah you're right Monkeyman.. I was reading the vent was up and could be pushed down. Not being held up by anything.  The deck lid sagging?  Hinge adjustment to where it bolts to the frame?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Standard||09-05-2000||05:33 AM||||You can adjust the latch on the decklid to make the it close tighter.  Should be 2 10 or 13 mm bolts that hold the latch on, just loosen those and push the latch up a bit.  <P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 150,000 miles and counting!       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">    <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||09-05-2000||06:00 AM||||The problem with mine (and apparently Ponyas, too) is just with one side.  I haven't tried to adjust mine yet (maybe next weekend) but I've thought all along that it looked more bowed than out of adjustment.  I'm beginning to wonder if there wasn't a bad run of these at the factory.<P>Ponya--What year is your car???||||reg||1
Z||000006||Haze_Performance||09-05-2000||06:41 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Monkeyman:<BR><B>The problem with mine (and apparently Ponyas, too) is just with one side.  I haven't tried to adjust mine yet (maybe next weekend) but I've thought all along that it looked more bowed than out of adjustment.  I'm beginning to wonder if there wasn't a bad run of these at the factory.<P>Ponya--What year is your car???</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Your right MM. Its wraped. Syryo86SE has the same problem with his. (His is bowed right by the drivers side engine vent) I tried to ajust it but no luck. Its just wraped.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycarsig.jpg">   <B>1985 Sport Coupe </B><P><BR><B>Website's  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/WS6_Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero</A> &                  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/HMP" TARGET=_blank>H.M.P. </A></B>||||reg||9
Z||000007||ponya||09-05-2000||10:38 PM||||Hey guys, just got finished reading all your posts. Sorry about the confusion regarding the vent. It's not the vent it's the hatch just where Monkeyman said it was, behind the driver. If that's the case, I think I'll just leave it alone. My luck,I'll loosen the two bolts and wont ever get it to close properly again. Thanks again,   Bob<BR>BTW MM my car is an 86 SE.||||reg||14
